 "findings": [
  {
   "gate": "U5 triangles equal / U10",
   "cause": "Unreal 5.8's static FBX import (Remove Degenerates, the default) drops every triangle with |cross|^2 < 1e-8 cm^4 (area < 0.005 mm^2; FbxStaticMeshImport.cpp GetTriangleAreaThreshold). gunlib.tspace.unreal_drops() predicts exactly Unreal's counts: SM_AR01 4,584 / 580 / 122 / 0 and SM_AR01_Mag 772 / 33 / 0 / 0 of LOD0-3 (the skeletal import keeps them: SK_AR01 has 3,812 / 547 / 122 / 0 such triangles). They are micro bevel and boolean run-out strips (4-25 microns wide) made by the part generators, plus decimation slivers at LOD1-2.",
   "effect": "triangle counts differ Blender / FBX vs Unreal; hairline cracks where the strips were (sub-pixel)"
  },
  {
   "gate": "U10",
   "cause": "'nearly zero tangents / bi-normals' (SM_AR01, SM_AR01_Mag) and 'degenerate tangent bases' (SM_AR01): StaticMeshBuild.cpp HasBadNTB on the render data. Unreal's exported render data (ASCII FBX) located them: 20 / 44 / 24 / 1 zero tangents on SM_AR01 LOD0-3 and 6 / 4 / 1 / 0 on SM_AR01_Mag; tangent = normal on 12 / 63 / 26 SM_AR01 LOD1-3 vertices. Causes: needle corners of the micro strips (float32 angle weight 0), faces seen edge-on by their shading normal, and LOD faces whose UV collapsed onto a line / point (island snapping).",
   "effect": "normal-map shading wrong at those few vertices (sub-pixel strips; LOD1-3 snapped faces)"
  },
  {
   "gate": "fix attempts (stage 8, generator side)",
   "result": "gunlib.tspace.unreal_safe (collapse micro edges, split needles, re-UV degenerate faces, tilt edge-on corner normals) made the test meshes import with 0 warnings, 0 dropped triangles and 0 zero tangents (TVB variants, ar_tan_ue.log), but as an export step it opened 3-face edges (qa_skeletal edge_manifold), moved vertices up to ~1 mm, pushed UVs out of their tile (uv0_inside_0_1) and multiplied the generated-lightmap overlaps (LOD0 85 -> 2,718 px at 1024); applied to the parts it broke G5 (butt gap 0.0074 mm, 3 LOD1 pairs) and the LOD-share targets (LOD0 shrank 8 %). A link-checked live-bmesh variant does not converge. Everything was reverted; the shipped bytes are the stage-7 geometry.",
   "recommendation": "change the method: remove the micro strips where the part generators make them (minimum bevel segment and boolean sliver >= 0.05 mm, triangles >= 0.01 mm^2, checked by unreal_drops() == 0 as a form-stage gate), and give LOD faces non-degenerate UVs at the LOD UV stage; then re-run stages 2-8."
  },
  {
   "gate": "U8 generated UV1 overlap",
   "cause": "Unreal's FLayoutUV output overlaps on this many-chart mesh: at the lightmap's own 64 px SM_AR01 LOD1-3 overlap 1 / 3 / 4 texels (LOD0 0), at 1024 px 85 / 77 / 53 / 53 (mag LOD0-1 22 / 190); the shipped UV0 and UV1 have 0 overlapping triangles (SAT test, lodfix.overlap_pairs). Higher minimum lightmap resolutions (256-1024) and full-precision UVs reduce but do not remove it (lmtest/).",
   "recommendation": "decide the lightmap route for static-lit buyers (plan R12): the authored UV1 with Generate Lightmap UVs off measured fewer overlaps (LOD0 11 px at 1024) but not zero either"
  },
  {
   "gate": "U5 bounds",
